  "prompt": "BUG: weisfeiler_lehman_graph_hash drops directed edge-label prefixes causing hash collisions\n\nWhen hashing a directed graph using `weisfeiler_lehman_graph_hash` with an `edge_attr` supplied, the function silently drops the `s_` (successor) and `p_` (predecessor) prefixes on the edge labels\n\nas a result, mathematically distinct directed graphs (such as an inward-pointing star and an outward-pointing star) incorrectly generate the exact same hash.\n\n### Reproducer\n```python\nimport networkx as nx\n\na = nx.DiGraph([(0, 1), (0, 2)]) # Outward star\nb = nx.DiGraph([(1, 0), (2, 0)]) # Inward star\n\nfor graph in [a, b]:\n    nx.set_edge_attributes(graph, \"e\", \"label\")\n\nhash_a = nx.weisfeiler_lehman_graph_hash(a, edge_attr=\"label\")\nhash_b = nx.weisfeiler_lehman_graph_hash(b, edge_attr=\"label\")\n\nprint(\"Hashes equal:\", hash_a == hash_b)",
